  },
  data: {
    LLM: "After deal, bidding starts with player to dealer's left (sitter). First speaker is to sitter's left. Bid 3 or pass; then pass or next number (4, 5, 6…). No jump bids. Only first round allows blind 2 (without looking). Declarer takes 4-card stock, discards 4 face-down (or plays without stock for doubled stakes). Declarer announces melds (melles: four of a kind, sequences; stoek: K-Q of trumps) before first lead (sequences) or by when Q of trumps is played (stoek). Declarer names trumps and leads. Follow suit or trump; jack of trumps never forced. Trick to highest trump, else highest of led suit. Winner leads next. Seven tricks.",
    Player: "After deal, bidding starts with player to dealer's left (sitter). First speaker is to sitter's left. Bid 3 or pass; then pass or next number (4, 5, 6…). No jump bids. Only first round allows blind 2 (without looking). Declarer takes 4-card stock, discards 4 face-down (or plays without stock for doubled stakes). Declarer announces melds (melles: four of a kind, sequences; stoek: K-Q of trumps) before first lead (sequences) or by when Q of trumps is played (stoek). Declarer names trumps and leads. Follow suit or trump; jack of trumps never forced. Trick to highest trump, else highest of led suit. Winner leads next. Seven tricks.",
    objective: 'As declarer, take at least the bid number of card points (in tricks plus stock and melds). Bids 3–6 mean 130–160+ points. Sitter forced to play if all pass (bid 1 = 110 points or concede for -10 game points).',
    gameplay: "After deal, bidding starts with player to dealer's left (sitter). First speaker is to sitter's left. Bid 3 or pass; then pass or next number (4, 5, 6…). No jump bids. Only first round allows blind 2 (without looking). Declarer takes 4-card stock, discards 4 face-down (or plays without stock for doubled stakes). Declarer announces melds (melles: four of a kind, sequences; stoek: K-Q of trumps) before first lead (sequences) or by when Q of trumps is played (stoek). Declarer names trumps and leads. Follow suit or trump; jack of trumps never forced. Trick to highest trump, else highest of led suit. Winner leads next. Seven tricks.",
    keyRules: [
      'Bidding: 3 = 130 pts, 4 = 140, 5 = 150, 6 = 160; pass or next number only.',
      'Declarer takes stock and discards 4, or plays without stock (double stakes).',
      'Sequences and fours announced before first lead; stoek (K-Q trumps) by Q of trumps.',
      'Follow suit or trump; may trump anytime; never forced to play jack of trumps.',
      '146 card points total (141 in cards + 5 for last trick); all seven tricks = +10 bonus.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Four players (or five with dealer sitting out each hand).',
      deck: '32 cards: A, K, Q, J, 10, 9, 8, 7 in clubs, spades, hearts, diamonds (French or Dutch indices).',
      equipment: 'Cards.',
      dealing: "First dealer: deal face-up clockwise until someone receives a jack. Then shuffle, player to dealer's right cuts. Deal clockwise: 3 cards to each player, 4 face-down in centre (stock), then 4 cards to each player. Everyone has 7 cards.",
    },
    turnFlow: "After deal, bidding starts with player to dealer's left (sitter). First speaker is to sitter's left. Bid 3 or pass; then pass or next number (4, 5, 6…). No jump bids. Only first round allows blind 2 (without looking). Declarer takes 4-card stock, discards 4 face-down (or plays without stock for doubled stakes). Declarer announces melds (melles: four of a kind, sequences; stoek: K-Q of trumps) before first lead (sequences) or by when Q of trumps is played (stoek). Declarer names trumps and leads. Follow suit or trump; jack of trumps never forced. Trick to highest trump, else highest of led suit. Winner leads next. Seven tricks.",
