    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 7 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: As declarer, take at least the bid number of card points (in tricks plus stock and melds). Bids 3–6 mean 130–160+ points. Sitter forced to play if all pass (bid 1 = 110 points or concede for -10 game points).',
      "Turn-flow example: After deal, bidding starts with player to dealer's left (sitter). First speaker is to sitter's left. Bid 3 or pass; then pass or next number (4, 5, 6…). No jump bids. Only first round allows blind 2 (without looking). Declarer takes 4-card stock, discards 4 face-down (or plays without stock for doubled stakes). Declarer announces melds (melles: four of a kind, sequences; stoek: K-Q of trumps) before first lead (sequences) or by when Q of trumps is played (stoek). Declarer names trumps and leads. Follow suit or trump; jack of trumps never forced. Trick to highest trump, else highest of led suit. Winner leads next. Seven tricks.",
      'Scoring example: Declarer wins or loses game points (1 game point ≈ 10 card points). Achieved: card points in tricks plus stock, rounded; +5 last trick; +10 bonus for all seven tricks. Required: bid + 10 minus (meld points ÷ 10). Win difference or lose 2×difference + 10; no stock doubles amount. Declarer must take at least the bid number of card points (tricks + stock + melds). Game points: achieved minus required; loss = 2×shortfall + 10..',
